<title>POLAND: NBP drains PLN 1.4 mln from Polish money market.</title>
<headline>NBP drains PLN 1.4 mln from Polish money market.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland drained 1.42 billion zlotys from the market through a reverse NBP-bill repurchase auction after banks bid to place 1.42 billion with the central bank, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The bank drained 856 million zlotys in a seven day reverse repo tender at an unchanged maximum rate of 23.45 percent and 568 million in a 14-day operation at an unchanged rate of 23.55 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 653 9700</p>
